{"timestamp":"2026-02-07T04:45:02","what_happened":"test_integration.py had sys.exit(0) at module level, preventing pytest from collecting tests. The file also had a function named 'test()' which pytest tried to run as a test fixture.","what_learned":"Never use sys.exit() at module level in test files — guard it with if __name__ == '__main__'. Never name helper functions 'test' in pytest-collected files. Use 'run_check' or similar.","applies_to":"testing pytest python","session_id":"opus46_mac_studio_session2"}
